      "value": "It's a good idea, but it can already be done better by being on green, but in an invite+ instance. At least that is how we do it. \n\nIt would be a weird concept when you have two friends, one on green and one on orange, while knowing they are in the same instance. With that information, you could join the orange person without getting invited. \n\nRight now you can not see their location, so direct joins are not possible. Exposing their location would also always allow you to join their instance directly unless it is invite-only, in which case your new status makes no sense. They would need to expose the world name but not the instance, and I doubt that this would be easy to add in the API.\n\nHonestly, the best you can do is set your personal status accordingly, like \"Playing Murder 4 right now\". What I would request instead is having this status automated (like `I'm in {WORLD_NAME} right now`, so you don't need to update it yourself whenever the world name changes.\n\nI made a canny to describe this better: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/add-variables-to-status-local-time-relative-time-current-world-name-etc",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
