  "details": "Sometimes, a friend or I are on orange so it requires an invite, but I don't want to let people request an invite without knowing where I am. I often won't make a request simply because I don't know what the friend might be doing. But if I saw that they were in a Murder 4 lobby, I'd be a lot more comfortable requesting off of them.\n\nIt still doesn't let people just join because it still requires an invitation, but it would at least give friends a better idea as to what you are doing before joining.\n\nImagining what this might look like in game, there would be a new status option between orange (ask me) and green (online) that is colored yellow. It might be labeled something like \"see me.\"\n\nSelecting this as a status hides you from the joinable friends tab in the social menu, but will still show your location on your profile like it would if you were on green or blue. A friend can see where you are and have a better idea as to what you're doing (sleeping, playing games, chilling, etc.). The friend then retains the option to request to join, the same as if you were on orange. You would receive the request and can choose to accept or decline or reply. The decline and reply options don't allow the person to join and the accept option sends the invitation.\n\nThe shown location will still display if there are mutual friends. If another friend with you is on blue or green status, another person would be able to join you without an invitation in the same way they would still be able to join you if you were on orange or red with a friend on blue or green.",
